From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: the AML card's surround71 alone is not a
 passthrough device

On S5/T7 and later every surround71 is marked HDMI, and the AML card's
carries only TrueHD and DTS-HD MA: the device check (at Kodi's start and
at every device change) and the passthrough device list leave it out by
name, so the setting points at the card's hdmi. That filter matched any
card's surround71, so with binaural's loopback (Virtual Sound) chosen for
passthrough, the check moved the device ActiveAE holds to the AML card's
iec958 until it next read the setting. A sink opened for passthrough in
between, as at a device change during a bitstream, opened the AML card:
the receiver played it directly, some 27 dB louder than through Virtual
Sound.

The filter now matches the AML card's surround71 alone; the loopback's
is checked and listed as any passthrough device is.

Shared code: CoreELEC put this AML filter in the device check
(ActiveAESink.cpp) and the list's filler (ActiveAESettings.cpp); both
filter by name before any sink is asked, so the AML sink cannot do it.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESettings.cpp |  3 ++-
 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp     | 15 +++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESettings.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESettings.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESettings.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESettings.cpp
@@ -180,7 +180,8 @@
     {
       // filter L-PCM device when passthrough on Amlogic T7, S5 or newer
       if (passthrough && filter_passthrough &&
-          StringUtils::StartsWith(sink->second, "ALSA:surround71"))
+          StringUtils::StartsWith(sink->second, "ALSA:surround71") &&
+          sink->second.find("AUGESOUND") != std::string::npos)
         continue;
 
       if (sink == sinkList.begin())
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp
@@ -758,6 +758,13 @@
   }
 }
 
+// the AML card's surround71 is its L-PCM device on S5/T7; another card's
+// (an ALSA loopback) is a passthrough device itself
+static bool IsAMLLPCMDevice(const std::string& name)
+{
+  return name.substr(0, name.find(':')) == "surround71" && name.find("AUGESOUND") != std::string::npos;
+}
+
 std::string CActiveAESink::ValidateOuputDevice(const std::string& device, bool passthrough) const
 {
   if (m_sinkInfoList.empty())
@@ -782,7 +789,7 @@
           continue;
 
         // filter L-PCM device when passthrough on Amlogic S5/T7
-        if (passthrough && (d.m_deviceName.substr(0, d.m_deviceName.find(':')) == "surround71"))
+        if (passthrough && IsAMLLPCMDevice(d.m_deviceName))
           continue;
 
         if (d.m_deviceName == dev.name)
@@ -808,7 +815,7 @@
           continue;
 
         // filter L-PCM device when passthrough on Amlogic S5/T7
-        if (passthrough && (d.m_deviceName.substr(0, d.m_deviceName.find(':')) == "surround71"))
+        if (passthrough && IsAMLLPCMDevice(d.m_deviceName))
           continue;
 
         if (d.GetFriendlyName() == dev.friendlyName)
@@ -836,7 +843,7 @@
           continue;
 
         // filter L-PCM device when passthrough on Amlogic S5/T7
-        if (passthrough && (d.m_deviceName.substr(0, d.m_deviceName.find(':')) == "surround71"))
+        if (passthrough && IsAMLLPCMDevice(d.m_deviceName))
           continue;
 
         if (firstDevice.empty())
@@ -869,7 +876,7 @@
         continue;
 
       // filter L-PCM device when passthrough on Amlogic S5/T7
-      if (passthrough && (d.m_deviceName.substr(0, d.m_deviceName.find(':')) == "surround71"))
+      if (passthrough && IsAMLLPCMDevice(d.m_deviceName))
         continue;
 
       if (firstDevice.empty())
